      {
        "id": 40692,
        "name": "Hex_Enduction_Hour",
        "username": "Hex_Enduction_Hour",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/hex_enduction_hour/{size}/2749_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-11T15:30:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I play SotM solitaire. Ihaven't yet fought all the villains, but am getting there!</p><p>Grand Warlord Voss on the Wagner Mars Base was quite fun. The narrative was exciting. I grew up a Kirby fan and reading the Avengers and Legion of Super-Heroes. The game I played against Voss brought back memories of those comics' galactic tales (Kree/Skrull, Thanos, Darkseid vs LoSH, etc.). I'd played on Wagner before, but had not experienced the self-destruct countdown card. &nbsp;In this game, I pulled it up and was floored with its creativity.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I'm in love with this game for its comic book roots, ability to play solo, strong narrative, and creative design. A big THANK YOU to the designers for creating such a fun experience!</p>",
        "post_number": 10,
        "post_type": 1,
